	Well I have traced the previous problem with the Makefile
to something that I did.  This is what I've expected was the problem
but just couldn't find it.  I put the touch makedefs.c in wrongly
because I am unfamiliar with makefile protocol.  
	Now however it fails with compilation errors in the following
way.  It proceeds normally for a bit then right after this line:
	cc -O -I../include -c apply.c
is printed then errors begin to crop up.  Here are a few of the first
lines:
	"apply.c", line 23 u undefined
	"apply.c", line 23 ux undefined
	"apply.c", member of structure or union required
and it continues till bombing with too many errors.
	It seems like a structure u is missing.  I found inside the
file include/you.h a structure called you and it seemed to have all
the same fields (like ux) that the compiler was complaining about.
I tried remnaming this structure to u but that made no difference 
at all so I restored the original file and have punted.  I did not
expect this to work anyway, an error like that would have been
impossible to miss.
	Is anybody else having this kind of difficulty on a Unix system
or is it just me?  Any other suggestions before I just rm the whole
collection of stuff and return to Omega?

